// Google sign-in on iOS (docs/decisions/0022-flutter-mobile-app.md, mobile/README.md).
//
// The Google SDK returns to the app through a URL scheme: the iOS OAuth client id reversed, for example
// com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abcdef for 1234567890-abcdef.apps.googleusercontent.com. Set it here to the
// reversed form of the id the build gets as --dart-define=GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID. A client id is a public identifier,
// not a secret, so the value may be committed. Set both or neither: the button appears when the dart-define is set,
// and without this scheme the Google SDK stops the app as soon as it is tapped.
GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID =
